---
title: "exec - transaction_execution (Sui Whitepaper: Transaction Effects)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_resolve: resolve function from CallTarget (package, module, function)
    q_resolve --> q_bind: bind type args, object args, value args to function params
    q_bind --> q_meter_init: initialize gas metering with MaxGas budget
    q_meter_init --> q_run_vm: execute function via Move VM

    q_run_vm --> q_check_gas_left: check remaining gas budget
    q_check_gas_left --> q_continue: gas remaining > 0
    q_check_gas_left --> q_abort_gas: gas budget exhausted
    q_abort_gas --> q_abort_effects: abort with no effects (deduct fees only)
    q_abort_effects --> [*]: return AbortEffects(abort_code, module_name)

    q_continue --> q_apply_effects: execution completes successfully
    q_continue --> q_abort_runtime: runtime abort (e.g. assertion failure)
    q_abort_runtime --> q_abort_effects

    q_apply_effects --> q_compute_fees: compute fees = (GasUsed * BaseFee) + Tip
    q_compute_fees --> q_deduct_gas: deduct fees from gas object (Coin of SUI)
    q_deduct_gas --> [*]: return SuccessEffects(Created, Mutated, Wrapped, Deleted, Events)

    note right of q_run_vm
        INV-001: Transaction execution has all-or-nothing semantics
        INV-002: Aborted transactions still charge gas fees
        INV-003: Output is deterministic given same inputs
        INV-004: Execution can proceed in parallel for causally unrelated transactions
    end note
